#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198110 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "02d2757f-1179-5ad6-b8c7-5165ac3a3eff" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability on a Bounded Interval"}] :question/id #uuid "3459a04b-bb14-54ff-aaea-976fa542e3e0" :question/math-academy-id "e-13269" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $\\Phi(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z \\sim N(0,1),$ compute $P(-0.53 <   Z <        0.53).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\, 0.02 \\,$ | $\\, 0.03 \\,$ | $\\, 0.04 \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\, 0.4 \\,$ | $\\, 0.6628 \\,$ | $\\, 0.6664 \\,$ | $\\, 0.67 \\,$ |\n| $\\, 0.5 \\,$ | $\\, 0.6985 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7019 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7054 \\,$ |\n| $\\, 0.6 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7324 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7357 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7389 \\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $Z\\sim N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(-0.53 <        Z <        0.53).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/bb86bde3595d6a64d1cd82da3c928f28c496f495f9c6815e56ee025a4a69d685.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $\\Phi(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z \\leq z) = \\Phi(z).\n$$\n\nSo, we express the required probability in terms of $\\Phi(z)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.53<Z<0.53) & =P(Z<0.53)-P(Z\\le -0.53) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 0.53)-P(Z\\le -0.53) \\\\  & =Φ(0.53)-Φ(-0.53)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we know that\n\n$$\n\\Phi(0.53) = 0.7019,\n$$\n\nbut we are not given $\\Phi(-0.53) .$ However, we can compute this using symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-0.53) & =P(Z\\le -0.53) \\\\  & =P(Z\\ge 0.53) \\\\  & =1-P(Z<0.53) \\\\  & =1-P(Z\\le 0.53) \\\\  & =1-Φ(0.53) \\\\  & =1-0.7019 \\\\  & =0.2981\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.53<Z<0.53) & =Φ(0.53)-Φ(-0.53) \\\\  & =0.7019-0.2981 \\\\  & =0.4038.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198111 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "27018e18-9368-5171-ae78-097adc8bcddf" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability on an Unbounded Interval"}] :question/id #uuid "3fe23c3b-29c8-5858-ae1d-b7a7aa34f76b" :question/math-academy-id "e-13270" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $\\Phi(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z \\sim N(0,1),$ compute $P(Z \\gt -0.76).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\, 0.05 \\,$ | $\\, 0.06 \\,$ | $\\, 0.07 \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\, 0.6 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7422 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7454 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7486 \\,$ |\n| $\\, 0.7 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7734 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7764 \\,$ | $\\, 0.7794 \\,$ |\n| $\\, 0.8 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8023 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8051 \\,$ | $\\, 0.8078 \\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/f88bf9a66694858e9eaf16f616555eda6d9da7de9f62b678bc1f03b32bf9a620.png)\n\nFor a random variable $Z \\sim N(0,1)$ we have the following symmetry property for $a > 0{:}$\n\n$$\nP(Z \\gt -a) = P(Z \\lt a) = \\Phi(a)\n$$\n\nWe're given that $Z\\sim N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P( Z > -0.76).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/fbacbbe3f53c73316fd070d95e4c077cd695bdcf884d30a95f6b0850df328c80.png)\n\nBy symmetry, this equals the area corresponding to the probability $P(Z \\lt 0.76).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/c0f612336c02eee97d6c66b56f0854286b3a23b90053810e9e4fb75b698b5a60.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(Z > -0.76)\n= P(Z < 0.76)\n= \\Phi(0.76)\n= 0.7764.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198112 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1a6ee4c7-a51f-5dce-b5c9-2e00acf6bf3e" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability on an Unbounded Interval Using the Complement"}] :question/id #uuid "8b0db808-0cb9-5feb-b405-4ebab693bee5" :question/math-academy-id "e-13271" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $\\Phi(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z \\sim N(0,1),$ compute $P(Z \\lt -1.54).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\, 0.02 \\,$ | $\\, 0.03 \\,$ | $\\, 0.04 \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\, 1.3 \\,$ | $\\, 0.9066 \\,$ | $\\, 0.9082 \\,$ | $\\, 0.9099 \\,$ |\n| $\\, 1.4 \\,$ | $\\, 0.9222 \\,$ | $\\, 0.9236 \\,$ | $\\, 0.9251 \\,$ |\n| $\\, 1.5 \\,$ | $\\, 0.9357 \\,$ | $\\, 0.9370 \\,$ | $\\, 0.9382 \\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/4d6524ff1e32b2c2b4aaf7481dbf63a96f847cd91ce66aeeb58690f37bbe50e5.png)\n\nFor a random variable $Z \\sim N(0,1),$ we have the following symmetry property for $a > 0{:}$\n\n$$\nP(Z \\gt a) = P(Z \\lt -a) = \\Phi(-a)\n$$\n\nWe're given that $Z\\sim N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P( Z \\lt -1.54).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/52d4c1add91819ff1f9dddf609b5753506c26e6cd6ee7f3cb14150ccb9b60971.png)\n\nBy symmetry, this equals the area corresponding to the probability $P(Z \\gt 1.54).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/7fef056bb5564986a009198685a2951de87ccb8e09c932c6902bfafdcdf0656f.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z<-1.54) & =P(Z>1.54) \\\\  & =1-P(Z<1.54) \\\\  & =1-Φ(1.54) \\\\  & =1-0.9382 \\\\  & =0.0618.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365297 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1a6ee4c7-a51f-5dce-b5c9-2e00acf6bf3e" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability on an Unbounded Interval Using the Complement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67b9bc74-9eea-5963-a2d1-dc5e233fb4b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2136" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365299} {:answer/id #uuid "32d799bf-a468-5ff8-b025-f5a1b7324f6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2327" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365300} {:answer/id #uuid "66a9b14a-2b51-5958-90b9-5563fbd4da08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2470" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365301} {:answer/id #uuid "f02e57b8-707b-5043-ab46-84ce68daf9c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7849" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365302} {:answer/id #uuid "65b6dec7-7bda-523a-8a16-471a09da941b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7673" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365303}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32d799bf-a468-5ff8-b025-f5a1b7324f6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2327" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365300} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2f5c906-45d7-5753-ba38-7ae8cd989afa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365298}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d0b4c1cd-9412-598a-85f5-bf3813ecf007" :question/math-academy-id "q-131532" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(Z<-0.73).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.7673\\,$ | $\\,0.7704\\,$ | $\\,0.7734\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.7967\\,$ | $\\,0.7995\\,$ | $\\,0.8023\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.9\\,$ | $\\,0.8238\\,$ | $\\,0.8264\\,$ | $\\,0.8289\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/597125714057269b7adf9c0a2a9bbdde9631cf37bc80518281ab4444c3189717.png)\n\nFor a random variable $Z∼N(0,1),$ we have the following symmetry property for $a>0:$\n\n$$\nP(Z>a)=P(Z<-a)=Φ(-a)\n$$\n\nWe're given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(Z<-0.73).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/3e4fb2143266d45a620bf39a978ba8ac4f0ed2585942f79dc90435a4896f9a0d.png)\n\nBy symmetry, this equals the area corresponding to the probability $P(Z>0.73).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/6bb24449a20276b9d190e2b31926bb6e0d52f22536431e27c05db00b92886ffc.png)\n\nNote that the two shaded areas above have the same area. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z<-0.73) & =P(Z>0.73) \\\\  & =1-P(Z<0.73) \\\\  & =1-Φ(0.73) \\\\  & =1-0.7673 \\\\  & =0.2327.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365304 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "27018e18-9368-5171-ae78-097adc8bcddf" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability on an Unbounded Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e9de8b39-10e6-5647-baf2-17085c313786" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0080" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365306} {:answer/id #uuid "d8760c3b-18f0-5be6-bebc-5982fabfda11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0107" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365307} {:answer/id #uuid "612d43b6-9913-5b0c-8070-8257715f1788" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0102" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365308} {:answer/id #uuid "29b46275-4137-51f7-a9c4-4059938c040f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0104" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365309} {:answer/id #uuid "84ac86ea-12b3-5d65-86e5-c3b5ba6e0358" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0060" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365310}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29b46275-4137-51f7-a9c4-4059938c040f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0104" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365309} :answer-field/id #uuid "39f936f5-6e65-5f20-b4b5-0517b54a2263" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365305}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e44bd541-9801-5aa0-9556-8f6a8293f5c2" :question/math-academy-id "q-183736" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(Z>2.31).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-2.5\\,$ | $\\,0.0062\\,$ | $\\,0.0060\\,$ | $\\,0.0059\\,$ |\n| $\\,-2.4\\,$ | $\\,0.0082\\,$ | $\\,0.0080\\,$ | $\\,0.0078\\,$ |\n| $\\,-2.3\\,$ | $\\,0.0107\\,$ | $\\,0.0104\\,$ | $\\,0.0102\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/f25b8fea7403579d1ee40cc00b9447e3362dc28c2e9d41f762f51df5e11daaf8.png)\n\nFor a random variable $Z∼N(0,1),$ we have the following symmetry property for $a>0:$\n\n$$\nP(Z>a)=P(Z<-a)=Φ(-a)\n$$\n\nWe're given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(Z>2.31).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/a3e01ca4fd737cea9afe95374a17c0428f83a6717d98a7557222a856aa2d0c02.png)\n\nBy symmetry, this equals the area corresponding to the probability $P(Z<-2.31).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/ce206061194e357b9cd75f9b260e4035a8600726a17cc0ee04ab39219bd45e94.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(Z>2.31)=P(Z<-2.31)=Φ(-2.31)=0.0104.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365311 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "27018e18-9368-5171-ae78-097adc8bcddf" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability on an Unbounded Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a79cd33a-21c2-58ba-9f51-0430ea2ee6b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8340" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365313} {:answer/id #uuid "e5b0e334-f33b-56a8-8a49-d2c56d1e50eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8289" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365314} {:answer/id #uuid "20ab3f21-aba7-545e-a1cf-7c972869112b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1711" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365315} {:answer/id #uuid "fb93fb5a-ad01-518e-a65d-afdea7ff09fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8577" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365316} {:answer/id #uuid "490e35c3-e374-545e-8dca-e4d22a051648" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1660" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365317}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a79cd33a-21c2-58ba-9f51-0430ea2ee6b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8340" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365313} :answer-field/id #uuid "5dd25558-7795-5694-8988-fef8bdee55c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365312}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b6302cc7-fd7e-5631-ae75-88056b993d4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-183745" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(Z>-0.97).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.8023\\,$ | $\\,0.8051\\,$ | $\\,0.8078\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.9\\,$ | $\\,0.8289\\,$ | $\\,0.8315\\,$ | $\\,0.8340\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.0\\,$ | $\\,0.8531\\,$ | $\\,0.8554\\,$ | $\\,0.8577\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/37674375730f32a70d7909a7ab01f3f9c836cf9c72d16447d499af20427f022c.png)\n\nFor a random variable $Z∼N(0,1)$ we have the following symmetry property for $a>0:$\n\n$$\nP(Z>-a)=P(Z<a)=Φ(a)\n$$\n\nWe're given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(Z>-0.97).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/a8b07524ca3a1ac1750f86e9a5088a07150d7d1b038158e74d924b8811a405a0.png)\n\nBy symmetry, this equals the area corresponding to the probability $P(Z<0.97).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/ef497f11f5ec451215e923157b6675d16c175dc23ec7d6576bf0a018e3ef594c.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(Z>-0.97)=P(Z<0.97)=Φ(0.97)=0.8340.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365318 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1a6ee4c7-a51f-5dce-b5c9-2e00acf6bf3e" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability on an Unbounded Interval Using the Complement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99123088-2cff-5b7a-aec0-a40a4210a8d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9505" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365320} {:answer/id #uuid "7ca6dbb7-ca81-5b08-81b1-948366ad5a6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9599" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365321} {:answer/id #uuid "edfa5f2a-0771-53e0-ab76-6c30e42589a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9495" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365322} {:answer/id #uuid "073c43d4-3aca-53b3-89da-c688085b5116" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9678" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365323} {:answer/id #uuid "ce52a240-8a57-52eb-af81-9ae6b5b2d44a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9484" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365324}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99123088-2cff-5b7a-aec0-a40a4210a8d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9505" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365320} :answer-field/id #uuid "15e88f5b-c7b7-59e5-b91a-6dc48182049f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365319}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5da7cb87-393b-5a7c-be80-23ae178faf1c" :question/math-academy-id "q-183811" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(Z<1.65).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-1.8\\,$ | $\\,0.0336\\,$ | $\\,0.0329\\,$ | $\\,0.0322\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.7\\,$ | $\\,0.0418\\,$ | $\\,0.0409\\,$ | $\\,0.0401\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.6\\,$ | $\\,0.0516\\,$ | $\\,0.0505\\,$ | $\\,0.0495\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/1b3a9a3891150ae0b187c79e2305d391f719898a9efe42b42e7bf0777d965aa3.png)\n\nFor a random variable $Z∼N(0,1)$ we have the following symmetry property for $a>0:$\n\n$$\nP(Z>-a)=P(Z<a)=Φ(a)\n$$\n\nWe're given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(Z<1.65).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/fd2f95626ff0a8f1aa59e94e18fddaae63216ee5962f4b7264ea952db76619b6.png)\n\nBy symmetry, this equals the area corresponding to the probability $P(Z>-1.65).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/94dfdaf777193a2a4b39e7e13c1297c3497c3d4dd474599a16a1bd4f559602b0.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z<1.65) & =P(Z>-1.65) \\\\  & =1-P(Z<-1.65) \\\\  & =1-Φ(-1.65) \\\\  & =1-0.0495 \\\\  & =0.9505.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365325 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "02d2757f-1179-5ad6-b8c7-5165ac3a3eff" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability on a Bounded Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14580e4c-86ea-57d7-81c8-f9a8ed14a9a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2206" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365327} {:answer/id #uuid "03a4258d-e31e-5b4e-8983-7cd0f21cf929" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1272" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365328} {:answer/id #uuid "ee2beae4-ad11-5c63-826d-5ef15baa7c18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2886" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365329} {:answer/id #uuid "2c0f7d7e-da31-57d6-9e0a-737052a11b40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2052" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365330} {:answer/id #uuid "d6472c0f-c392-55de-af87-b1d37a685741" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1428" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365331}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d6472c0f-c392-55de-af87-b1d37a685741" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1428" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365331} :answer-field/id #uuid "f26c2fee-bfc4-5dec-803b-dc97d391f5a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365326}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d2b1b3dd-3aa5-58f9-8266-775ea952a8bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-183823" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(-0.18<Z<0.18).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.3594\\,$ | $\\,0.3557\\,$ | $\\,0.3520\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.3974\\,$ | $\\,0.3936\\,$ | $\\,0.3897\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.1\\,$ | $\\,0.4364\\,$ | $\\,0.4325\\,$ | $\\,0.4286\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(-0.18<Z<0.18).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/061aec33cb30172ec64c89841fc70cb2e5bec9b89f92ef0427ff9673bfa99219.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=Φ(z).\n$$\n\nSo, we express the required probability in terms of $Φ(z)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.18<Z<0.18) & =P(Z<0.18)-P(Z\\le -0.18) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 0.18)-P(Z\\le -0.18) \\\\  & =Φ(0.18)-Φ(-0.18)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we know that\n\n$$\nΦ(-0.18)=0.4286,\n$$\n\nbut we are not given $Φ(0.18).$ However, we can compute this using symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(0.18) & =P(Z\\le 0.18) \\\\  & =P(Z\\ge -0.18) \\\\  & =1-P(Z<-0.18) \\\\  & =1-P(Z\\le -0.18) \\\\  & =1-Φ(-0.18) \\\\  & =1-0.4286 \\\\  & =0.5714\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.18<Z<0.18) & =Φ(0.18)-Φ(-0.18) \\\\  & =0.5714-0.4286 \\\\  & =0.1428.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365332 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "02d2757f-1179-5ad6-b8c7-5165ac3a3eff" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability on a Bounded Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "874f1411-1489-5381-ad31-2981f2f207af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2118" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365334} {:answer/id #uuid "9150e487-f36f-5dd4-9761-ee2d7044a881" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2205" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365335} {:answer/id #uuid "78c08721-b5fb-5376-bdff-779f7ca32059" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2233" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365336} {:answer/id #uuid "a245f0d2-05e2-5b90-b9bf-b9d3808a81ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2167" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365337} {:answer/id #uuid "5d077201-d6f6-5a0c-aedf-e379c25c4206" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2231" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365338}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78c08721-b5fb-5376-bdff-779f7ca32059" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2233" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365336} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea06906b-8fd5-510b-a37e-59e231c5d765" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365333}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5580ddf0-d280-55cd-87b0-06ddfbc57e68" :question/math-academy-id "q-183828" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(-0.19<Z<0.38).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ | $\\,0.09\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.3557\\,$ | $\\,0.3520\\,$ | $\\,0.3483\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.3936\\,$ | $\\,0.3897\\,$ | $\\,0.3859\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.1\\,$ | $\\,0.4325\\,$ | $\\,0.4286\\,$ | $\\,0.4247\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(-0.19<Z<0.38).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/bd478e9925303e3d018e2d070e4e3a78e72fb699a48ac3109ddf743158bb5599.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=Φ(z).\n$$\n\nSo, we express the required probability in terms of $Φ(z)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.19<Z<0.38) & =P(Z<0.38)-P(Z\\le -0.19) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 0.38)-P(Z\\le -0.19) \\\\  & =Φ(0.38)-Φ(-0.19)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-0.38) & =0.3520 \\\\ Φ(-0.19) & =0.4247,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nbut we are not given $Φ(0.38).$ However, we can compute this using symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(0.38) & =P(Z\\le 0.38) \\\\  & =P(Z\\ge -0.38) \\\\  & =1-P(Z<-0.38) \\\\  & =1-P(Z\\le -0.38) \\\\  & =1-Φ(-0.38) \\\\  & =1-0.3520 \\\\  & =0.6480\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.19<Z<0.38) & =Φ(0.38)-Φ(-0.19) \\\\  & =0.6480-0.4247 \\\\  & =0.2233.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365339 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "27018e18-9368-5171-ae78-097adc8bcddf" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability on an Unbounded Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f156006-40e7-59ee-9535-6dbf94bf76cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3707" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365341}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f156006-40e7-59ee-9535-6dbf94bf76cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3707" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365341} :answer-field/id #uuid "2aa7a600-0f23-5000-a8c3-fea3674abbed" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365340}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d0f3f056-0037-536c-89b7-4c45bb247762" :question/math-academy-id "q-330631" :question/problem "| $z$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.3783\\,$ | $\\,0.3745\\,$ | $\\,0.3707\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.4168\\,$ | $\\,0.4129\\,$ | $\\,0.4090\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.1\\,$ | $\\,0.4562\\,$ | $\\,0.4522\\,$ | $\\,0.4483\\,$ |\n\nThe data above is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(Z>0.33).$ Use the table above and do not round your answer.\n\n$P(Z>0.33)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Acad