$\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.7704\\,$ | $\\,0.7734\\,$ | $\\,0.7764\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.7995\\,$ | $\\,0.8023\\,$ | $\\,0.8051\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.9\\,$ | $\\,0.8264\\,$ | $\\,0.8289\\,$ | $\\,0.8315\\,$ |\n\nThe data above is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function  $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(Z>-0.86).$ Use the table above and do not round your answer.\n\n$P(Z>-0.86)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/dc28d78d3f9334aad287ba8e3532b95e4287b84b395d58301016bb056dff2006.png)\n\nFor a random variable $Z∼N(0,1)$ we have the following symmetry property for $a>0:$\n\n$$\nP(Z>-a)=P(Z<a)=Φ(a)\n$$\n\nWe're given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(Z>-0.86).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/07d788a65e5a5c177e7d1e54a3212c71eb0b36f22ec9f582ebb3ad37c6de8cb7.png)\n\nBy symmetry, this equals the area corresponding to the probability $P(Z<0.86).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/abdde6b554257a3ed44d091a9a87095af7bde7534b0695f5ac97d6bf24bcb160.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(Z>-0.86)=P(Z<0.86)=Φ(0.86)=0.8051.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365346 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "27018e18-9368-5171-ae78-097adc8bcddf" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability on an Unbounded Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e04c705-2510-542d-8f20-a51d2e8f20b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7704" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365348}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e04c705-2510-542d-8f20-a51d2e8f20b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :