d "1a6ee4c7-a51f-5dce-b5c9-2e00acf6bf3e" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability on an Unbounded Interval Using the Complement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba222826-3036-5759-b6c5-48cfe6b78738" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.0516" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365351} {:answer/id #uuid "cacf34bb-97c5-514a-92ac-e5528e3a86ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9484" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365352}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cacf34bb-97c5-514a-92ac-e5528e3a86ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9484" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365352} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7a748f4-0e6a-5ba2-bcc5-082f9a9a5d9d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365350}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "100cc2c2-3a44-5594-9e6c-a56cfba54a9e" :question/math-academy-id "q-330650" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(Z<1.63).$ Use the table below and do not round your answer.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-1.7\\,$ | $\\,0.0436\\,$ | $\\,0.0427\\,$ | $\\,0.0419\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.6\\,$ | $\\,0.0537\\,$ | $\\,0.0526\\,$ | $\\,0.0516\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.5\\,$ | $\\,0.0655\\,$ | $\\,0.0643\\,$ | $\\,0.0630\\,$ |\n\n$P(Z<1.63)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/967a47f879a672d2b66c9ba1bac8ae3ddea220212ced411ccf382301f3c4b56e.png)\n\nFor a random variable $Z∼N(0,1)$ we have the following symmetry property for $a>0:$\n\n$$\nP(Z>-a)=P(Z<a)=Φ(a)\n$$\n\nWe're given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(Z<1.63).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/11598fe8ebdf6e04b11bc1a41a887378c1dfa8a5136b970328411325eccb5a50.png)\n\nBy symmetry, this equals the area corresponding to the probability $P(Z>-1.63).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/de76fcee7abfd8b2374c2ddc5f038114181ac60fcdbed08ad335f15d196c79a0.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z<1.63) & =P(Z>-1.63) \\\\  & =1-P(Z<-1.63) \\\\  & =1-Φ(-1.63) \\\\  & =1-0.0516 \\\\  & =0.9484.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365353 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1a6ee4c7-a51f-5dce-b5c9-2e00acf6bf3e" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability on an Unbounded Interval Using the Complement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4bec2373-43a9-5043-8a6d-a21b65b12d70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9738" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365355}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4bec2373-43a9-5043-8a6d-a21b65b12d70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9738" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365355} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ed6df51-3285-5f85-85d2-b8d4da50e504" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365354}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "53e3344a-2bac-51b5-a516-8529f57987f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-330651" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(Z<1.94).$ Use the table below and do not round your answer.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-2.0\\,$ | $\\,0.0224\\,$ | $\\,0.0217\\,$ | $\\,0.0212\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.9\\,$ | $\\,0.0274\\,$ | $\\,0.0268\\,$ | $\\,0.0262\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.8\\,$ | $\\,0.0344\\,$ | $\\,0.0336\\,$ | $\\,0.0329\\,$ |\n\n$P(Z<1.94)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/0316b85ed769fd2688538ed2c9a47236db0890bf52bf7fcbad021f7d509373b4.png)\n\nFor a random variable $Z∼N(0,1)$ we have the following symmetry property for $a>0:$\n\n$$\nP(Z>-a)=P(Z<a)=Φ(a)\n$$\n\nWe're given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(Z<1.94).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/e708b9dc6927a17f193c216f1b14b1b9ef98e6d9d26a998790112863661ca5d0.png)\n\nBy symmetry, this equals the area corresponding to the probability $P(Z>-1.94).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/43f1e2eb5354cbdcd5ff359985048fa2d6411167ad5f50fe45c730642e184b61.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z<1.94) & =P(Z>-1.94) \\\\  & =1-P(Z<-1.94) \\\\  & =1-Φ(-1.94) \\\\  & =1-0.0262 \\\\  & =0.9738.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365356 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1a6ee4c7-a51f-5dce-b5c9-2e00acf6bf3e" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability on an Unbounded Interval Using the Complement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd4d7fb5-a796-58ff-828c-e8476b666444" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3520" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365358}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd4d7fb5-a796-58ff-828c-e8476b666444" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3520" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365358} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7d20c04-327b-52a3-be58-2634dcf36eaf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365357}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c3481bdc-6bb2-5583-85be-5c9f6c24be0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-330661" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(Z<-0.38).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ | $\\,0.09\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.6064\\,$ | $\\,0.6103\\,$ | $\\,0.6141\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.6443\\,$ | $\\,0.6480\\,$ | $\\,0.6517\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.4\\,$ | $\\,0.6808\\,$ | $\\,0.6844\\,$ | $\\,0.6879\\,$ |\n\n$P(Z<-0.38)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/8a6467813ccf982906fb5d1d8cd5c5c88b984c22a1e238715c65315a7772249c.png)\n\nFor a random variable $Z∼N(0,1),$ we have the following symmetry property for $a>0:$\n\n$$\nP(Z>a)=P(Z<-a)=Φ(-a)\n$$\n\nWe're given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(Z<-0.38).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/ee2aebec9953a09dca6eab5c7e5434240885a383a6701638fffdaa9ee9cfeb40.png)\n\nBy symmetry, this equals the area corresponding to the probability $P(Z>0.38).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/619fae52bde8b2da729095f733e1ea1411132fffe70cc23e252a83cbb2e7ff23.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z<-0.38) & =P(Z>0.38) \\\\  & =1-P(Z<0.38) \\\\  & =1-Φ(0.38) \\\\  & =1-0.6480 \\\\  & =0.3520.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365359 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "02d2757f-1179-5ad6-b8c7-5165ac3a3eff" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability on a Bounded Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ee43f02-a302-595a-b20e-7372e1a8c914" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7357" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365361} {:answer/id #uuid "736bb855-85f4-5f7b-bc75-ee71606f7691" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4714" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365362}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "736bb855-85f4-5f7b-bc75-ee71606f7691" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4714" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365362} :answer-field/id #uuid "714a5d94-1904-53e6-9913-a93da697a8da" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365360}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9a135d73-fe19-5a20-b342-e8c19175fb17" :question/math-academy-id "q-330889" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(-0.63<Z<0.63).$ Use the table below and do not round your answer.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.4\\,$ | $\\,0.6628\\,$ | $\\,0.6664\\,$ | $\\,0.6700\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.5\\,$ | $\\,0.6985\\,$ | $\\,0.7019\\,$ | $\\,0.7054\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.6\\,$ | $\\,0.7324\\,$ | $\\,0.7357\\,$ | $\\,0.7389\\,$ |\n\n$P(-0.63<Z<0.63)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(-0.63<Z<0.63).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/09754e3068e550f6ba2a457f124828932408d0298ca163d6ad22e1caac51c2d0.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=Φ(z).\n$$\n\nSo, we express the required probability in terms of $Φ(z)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.63<Z<0.63) & =P(Z<0.63)-P(Z\\le -0.63) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 0.63)-P(Z\\le -0.63) \\\\  & =Φ(0.63)-Φ(-0.63).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we know that\n\n$$\nΦ(0.63)=0.7357,\n$$\n\nbut we are not given $Φ(-0.63).$ However, we can compute this using symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-0.63) & =P(Z\\le -0.63) \\\\  & =P(Z\\ge 0.63) \\\\  & =1-P(Z<0.63) \\\\  & =1-P(Z\\le 0.63) \\\\  & =1-Φ(0.63) \\\\  & =1-0.7357 \\\\  & =0.2643\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.63<Z<0.63) & =Φ(0.63)-Φ(-0.63) \\\\  & =0.7357-0.2643 \\\\  & =0.4714.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365363 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "02d2757f-1179-5ad6-b8c7-5165ac3a3eff" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability on a Bounded Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2a09873-72ae-5563-a018-35a6603b5255" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8788" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365365}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2a09873-72ae-5563-a018-35a6603b5255" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8788" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365365} :answer-field/id #uuid "351940d9-74b5-510b-a5c5-d01f13c46569" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365364}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c14c23d5-7455-50af-9191-550faf7f7f76" :question/math-academy-id "q-330903" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(-1.55<Z<1.55).$ Use the table below and do not round your answer.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,1.4\\,$ | $\\,0.9236\\,$ | $\\,0.9251\\,$ | $\\,0.9265\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.5\\,$ | $\\,0.9370\\,$ | $\\,0.9382\\,$ | $\\,0.9394\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.6\\,$ | $\\,0.9484\\,$ | $\\,0.9495\\,$ | $\\,0.9505\\,$ |\n\n$P(-1.55<Z<1.55)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(-1.55<Z<1.55).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/45d71abed85d91a5a1b150fb741bcc8fa9967f7b2b8d77df35423a909b1e8522.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=Φ(z).\n$$\n\nSo, we express the required probability in terms of $Φ(z)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-1.55<Z<1.55) & =P(Z<1.55)-P(Z\\le -1.55) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 1.55)-P(Z\\le -1.55) \\\\  & =Φ(1.55)-Φ(-1.55)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we know that\n\n$$\nΦ(1.55)=0.9394,\n$$\n\nbut we are not given $Φ(-1.55).$ However, we can compute this using symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-1.55) & =P(Z\\le -1.55) \\\\  & =P(Z\\ge 1.55) \\\\  & =1-P(Z<1.55) \\\\  & =1-P(Z\\le 1.55) \\\\  & =1-Φ(1.55) \\\\  & =1-0.9394 \\\\  & =0.0606\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-1.55<Z<1.55) & =Φ(1.55)-Φ(-1.55) \\\\  & =0.9394-0.0606 \\\\  & =0.8788.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365366 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "02d2757f-1179-5ad6-b8c7-5165ac3a3eff" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability on a Bounded Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d2e05292-35cc-59ef-997f-c5e5bcd4c75f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8764" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365368}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2e05292-35cc-59ef-997f-c5e5bcd4c75f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8764" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365368} :answer-field/id #uuid "940d9bb0-2b28-5602-89ff-31cf3b00c86d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365367}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f31e8083-0326-52b0-a159-f48c24746347" :question/math-academy-id "q-330908" :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(-1.54<Z<1.54).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-1.6\\,$ | $\\,0.0526\\,$ | $\\,0.0516\\,$ | $\\,0.0505\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.5\\,$ | $\\,0.0643\\,$ | $\\,0.0630\\,$ | $\\,0.0618\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.4\\,$ | $\\,0.0778\\,$ | $\\,0.0764\\,$ | $\\,0.0749\\,$ |\n\n$P(-1.54<Z<1.54)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(-1.54<Z<1.54).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/af13b1b1ef963dc2a922eab8b213015bd5af23b28fbf907fe4b7e5226a8768f4.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=Φ(z).\n$$\n\nSo, we express the required probability in terms of $Φ(z)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-1.54<Z<1.54) & =P(Z<1.54)-P(Z\\le -1.54) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 1.54)-P(Z\\le -1.54) \\\\  & =Φ(1.54)-Φ(-1.54)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we know that\n\n$$\nΦ(-1.54)=0.0618,\n$$\n\nbut we are not given $Φ(1.54).$ However, we can compute this using symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(1.54) & =P(Z\\le 1.54) \\\\  & =1-P(Z\\le -1.54) \\\\  & =1-Φ(-1.54) \\\\  & =1-0.0618 \\\\  & =0.9382\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-1.54<Z<1.54) & =Φ(1.54)-Φ(-1.54) \\\\  & =0.9382-0.0618 \\\\  & =0.8764.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
